step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple mean combination on the full pool to establish a baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse-error combination on the full pool to see if simple weighting improves over mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full model pool to see if it improves over mean/weighted.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean with 20% trimming on the full pool to see if it improves on the median baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled_meta_model handle (w1) on the full model pool to see if a learned meta weighting improves over simple inverse-error weighting.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse‑error combination on the smaller, high‑quality pool1 to see if restricting models improves performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Try a simple mean combination on the smaller, high‑quality pool1 to see if restricting models improves over median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","models":["rf","catboost","DWT_rf","FT_catboost","ONLY_DWT_catboost"]}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the same high‑quality pool4 to see if it outperforms the mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse‑error combination on the high‑quality pool4 to see if weighting improves over the median baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean combination on the high‑quality pool1 to see if restricting models improves over the current best median pool4.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a DBA (Dynamic Bayesian Aggregation) on the high‑quality pool1 to see if it can beat the current median‑pool4 baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse‑error combination on pool2 to see if adding the extra two models improves over the current median pool4 leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

